          :host {
            display: block;
            font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
          }

          .header {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.6rem;
            width: 100%;
            padding: 0.5rem 0;
            border: 0;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc;
            background: none;
            color: inherit;
            font: inherit;
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            text-align: left;
            cursor: pointer;
          }

          .indicator {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            display: inline-grid;
            place-items: center;
            width: 1.25rem;
            height: 1.25rem;
            border: 1px solid currentColor;
            line-height: 1;
          }

          .content {
            padding-top: 0.5rem;
          }

          .toggle {
            margin-top: 0.75rem;
            cursor: pointer;
          }
        </style>

        <button class="header" type="button" aria-expanded="false"
                aria-controls="details">
          <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          <slot name="header"></slot>
        </button>

        <div class="content">
          <slot name="intro"></slot>
          <div id="details" hidden>
            <slot name="details"></slot>
          </div>
          <button class="toggle" type="button">expand more</button>
        </div>
      `;

      this.headerButton = shadow.querySelector(".header");
      this.indicator = shadow.querySelector(".indicator");
      this.details = shadow.querySelector("#details");
      this.toggleButton = shadow.querySelector(".toggle");

      this.headerButton.addEventListener("click", () => this.toggle());
      this.toggleButton.addEventListener("click", () => this.toggle());
    }

    toggle() {
      const expanded = this.details.hidden;
      this.details.hidden = !expanded;
      this.headerButton.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(expanded));
      this.indicator.textContent = expanded ? "−" : "+";
      this.toggleButton.textContent = expanded ? "collapse" : "expand more";
    }
  }

  customElements.define("x-details", XDetails);
</script>
```

### Evaluation

Assistant A is much closer to a working solution. It uses Shadow DOM and slots correctly, keeps the intro visible, hides the details initially, and provides the requested indicator, header styling, and expand button. However, clicking the square toggles twice: the indicator has its own click handler, and that click bubbles to the header, which also toggles. As a result, clicking the square does not change the state. The header is also not keyboard-accessible.

Assistant B has fundamental implementation problems. It never calls `attachShadow()`, so `this.shadowRoot` is `null` and its `connectedCallback()` fails when trying to set `innerHTML`. It also does not create a shadow-DOM slot structure for the header, intro, or details. Its claim that a left border implements a `+`/`−` square is incorrect, and its styling does not provide the requested header bottom border. Even aside from the initial error, its click handlers do not actually implement working expand/collapse behavior.

Both answers could be clearer about the expanded-state button behavior, but A provides a substantially more complete and functional starting point. Assistant B’s code fails at initialization and misses several key requirements.

My final verdict is: [[A>>B]]

